This may incur some unnecessary `PropagateConstant` function calls. Imagine cases like `Proj -> Sel1 -> Sel2 -> Sel3 -> DataSource`, we may call `PropagateConstant` 3 times now, while only the last round is enough actually.

Also, we should make `Conds2TableDual` be aware of prepare plan cache. For example, if plan cache is enabled:
```
create table t(a varchar(8), b varchar(8));
insert into t values('1','1');
prepare stmt from "select count(1) from t where a = ? and a = ?";
set @p0 = '1', @p1 = '2';
execute stmt using @p0, @p1; -- 0 is returned.
set @p0 = '1', @p1 = '1';
execute stmt using @p0, @p1; -- 0 is returned which is wrong, because it reuses the TableDual plan generated in first execute.
```
